WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.930
In 1980, about 108 million
adults worldwide had diabetes.

2
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.520
By 2014, the number was 422 million.

3
00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:14.040
Part of that rise is a
bigger, older population.

4
00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:17.600
In each of them, blood
glucose stays too high.

5
00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.460
Yet two people can both
have high blood sugar,

6
00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:22.710
while only one lacks insulin.

7
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.180
How can that be?

8
00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:28.020
In this mission, you'll compare
the two main types of diabetes,

9
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.170
and what goes wrong in each.

10
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.080
Then you'll see how each type is treated.

11
00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:38.020
Your mission: find out how two people
can both have high blood sugar when only

12
00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.550
one lacks insulin.
